WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.398
Observation data should remain connected to mission context.

00:00:03.398 --> 00:00:08.757
Use consistent file names that include a date, mission identifier, platform or sensor,

00:00:08.757 --> 00:00:09.581
and sequence.

00:00:09.581 --> 00:00:13.291
Avoid generic names that lose meaning after files move.

00:00:13.291 --> 00:00:17.825
Preserve available metadata such as capture time, location, altitude estimate, orientation,

00:00:17.825 --> 00:00:21.535
device, and camera settings when the mission requires it.

00:00:21.535 --> 00:00:26.070
Metadata is useful context but can be incomplete, altered, or imprecise,

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:29.780
so it should not be treated as absolute proof.

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:34.726
Flight logs and source notes should record objective, crew, equipment, route, weather,

00:00:34.726 --> 00:00:37.200
lighting, settings, deviations, and significant events.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:43.795
Map references link images to the area of interest and help reviewers understand coverage and gaps.

00:00:43.795 --> 00:00:46.268
Protect original imagery from accidental editing.

00:00:46.268 --> 00:00:49.978
Store working copies, annotations, crops, and processed products separately,

00:00:49.978 --> 00:00:51.215
and document transformations.

00:00:51.215 --> 00:00:56.986
Every observation in a report should point to the relevant original or controlled derivative.

00:00:56.986 --> 00:00:59.459
Storage and access should reflect sensitivity.

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:03.581
Imagery may reveal private property, people, infrastructure, or operational details.

00:01:03.581 --> 00:01:07.704
Use approved encrypted storage and transfer where appropriate, restrict access,

00:01:07.704 --> 00:01:09.352
and log significant exports.

00:01:09.352 --> 00:01:13.062
Retention should match mission, policy, legal, and evidentiary needs.

00:01:13.062 --> 00:01:17.597
Remove unnecessary data through approved processes when the retention period ends.

00:01:17.597 --> 00:01:23.780
Good documentation makes analysis repeatable without turning a limited mission into an indefinite surveillance archive.
